{
  "about": "Diagram fields Mosaic adds to JSON Canvas, and how to draw them. Read by the write validator (validate.rs), the Rust renderer (render.rs) and the canvas editor (ui/src/diagrams/shapes.tsx), and documented in docs/AGENTS.md. A node without \"shape\" is an ordinary card. \"group\" sorts shapes in the Shape menu. \"draw\": rect (corner radius or \"pill\"), ellipse, or path (100×100 box, stretched; extra = unfilled lines; inset = label margin as a fraction), special figures (timing: lines \"Lane: State@0 Other@5\", optional \"time: 0..20 s\"), solid (filled with the line colour), hollow (no fill), label false (a symbol), behind (drawn under other cards), decor (an 18×18 UML icon top right), compartments (class box). \"icons\": inner SVG of 24×24 Lucide icons for a card's \"icon\". \"routes\": how a connection is drawn (orthogonal = around other cards).",
